CORE
main.c
--datarace --no-assertions --own-view-reads --no-por --unwind 4 --rounds 2 --allow-pointer-unsoundness
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
slot[] is written only before the spawn, so --own-view-reads gives the exact
pointers and main's slot[j]->next becomes `p == &b ? b..next : a..next`: the
last branch is a real object, not the unknown one. Read with the plain guard,
main read a..next on every path (and, under the last link alone, when p was &c) and was paired with the thread writing it
under the other mutex (goblint-regression/09-regions_11-arraylist_nr). The
last branch is read under the negation of the last link.
